          "text": "Agitation and behavioural episodes"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports agitation, irritability and difficulty concentrating at work and home; gets “really wound up,” especially with noise, changes in routine and unexpected instructions. Episodes occur most days and include pacing, talking fast and slamming doors. Reports punching walls or boxes; denies physical aggression toward others and says, “I’d never hit anyone just need to hit something.”"
      }
